# Spec Helper Extraction Policy

## Purpose

Specs must read as user scenarios.

Reusable technical logic must not live in `.spec.ts` files as local functions.

Agents must search existing project helpers before creating new ones.

---

## Core Principle

**Spec owns the scenario.**

**Helper owns reusable technical mechanics.**

Before adding any helper logic, check whether an equivalent already exists under `src/test/**`.

---

## Reuse-Before-Create Checklist

Before writing helper logic in a spec or creating a new helper file, search:

```text
src/test/assertions/**     — contract, invariant, stability, UI/API assertions
src/test/reporting/**      — Allure metadata, suite path builders
src/test/data/**           — builders, datasets, generators, types
src/test/pages/**          — Page Object actions and state readers
src/test/components/**     — Component Object actions and state readers
src/test/setup/**          — approved setup orchestration
src/test/schemas/**        — Zod/runtime contracts
```

If an existing helper covers the same responsibility, reuse or extend it.

Do not duplicate:

- Allure suite path builders;
- stability polling / signature waits;
- sort/filter/search invariant checks;
- schema validation wrappers;
- auth failure or response-shape assertions;
- reporting metadata mechanics.

When extending an existing helper is clearer than creating a parallel file, extend the existing helper.

---

## Forbidden In Spec Files

Do not define local functions in specs for:

- `run*Scenario`, `execute*Flow`, `perform*Workflow` orchestration;
- `waitForStable*`, signature polling, or other synchronization mechanics;
- `buildAllureSuitePath` or other reporting path builders;
- parsing, normalization, comparison, or sorting algorithms;
- reusable predicate checks used by multiple tests;
- schema validation plumbing;
- repeated request/response assertion blocks.

Matrix or table-driven tests must still keep `test.step`, actions, and verification visible inside each `test(...)` body.

### Bad

```ts
async function runVisibleProductSearchScenario(catalogPage, queryCase, submitSearch) {
  await applyAllureMetadata({ ... });
  await test.step("Search", async () => submitSearch(catalogPage, queryCase.q));
  await test.step("Verify", async () => {
    const names = await waitForStableVisibleProductSearchMatch(catalogPage, queryCase.q);
    expectVisibleProductSearchMatch(names, queryCase.q);
  });
}

test("...", async ({ catalogPage }) => {
  await runVisibleProductSearchScenario(catalogPage, queryCase, ...);
});
```

### Good

```ts
test("...", async ({ catalogPage }) => {
  await applyAllureMetadata({
    story: `${queryCase.label} (q=${queryCase.q})`,
    suite: buildAllureSuitePath(ROOT_SUITE, "Matching queries"),
    severity: "CRITICAL",
  });

  await test.step(`Search for ${queryCase.q}`, async () => {
    await catalogPage.searchByButton(queryCase.q);
  });

  await test.step("Verify visible products match the search query", async () => {
    const names = await waitForStableVisibleProductSearchMatch(catalogPage, queryCase.q);
    expectVisibleProductSearchMatch(names, queryCase.q);
  });
});
```

---

## Allowed In Spec Files

Specs may contain:

- imports;
- feature/suite constants such as `FEATURE`, `ROOT_SUITE`;
- small deterministic scenario arrays used only in that spec;
- `test.describe`, `test.beforeEach`, `test`, `test.step`;
- calls to Page Objects, builders, datasets, generators, fixtures, reporting helpers, assertion helpers;
- direct scenario-specific assertions that are not reusable.

Local functions in specs are forbidden by default.

The only narrow exception is a truly one-off helper that is:

- used once in the same file;
- at most three lines;
- not hiding the action under test;
- not likely to be reused;
- not technical parsing/comparison/sync logic.

If unsure, extract to the correct layer instead of keeping a local function.

---

## Helper Placement

| Responsibility | Preferred location |
|---|---|
| response shape validation | `src/test/schemas/api/**` |
| reusable API/UI assertions | `src/test/assertions/api/**`, `src/test/assertions/ui/**` |
| sort/filter/search invariants | `src/test/assertions/**` |
| UI stability polling | `src/test/assertions/ui/*-stability.helper.ts` |
| Allure metadata and suite paths | `src/test/reporting/allure-metadata.helper.ts` |
| reusable payloads/forms | `src/test/data/builders/**` |
| reusable scenario cases | `src/test/data/datasets/**` |
| unique primitive values | `src/test/data/generators/**` |
| locators and user actions | Page Objects / Component Objects |
| setup orchestration | `src/test/setup/**` |

Do not create new top-level helper folders without a real grouping need.

Prefer extending an existing helper in the same domain over creating a near-duplicate.

---

## Matrix And Table-Driven Tests

Allowed:

- loop over dataset in `test.describe` or `test(...)` declaration;
- shared `beforeEach` for safe navigation only;
- repeated `test.step` blocks inside each generated test.

Not allowed:

- local scenario runner that hides steps, actions, or assertions;
- moving matrix orchestration into spec-local functions;
- hiding the primary action under test inside a helper because the suite is parameterized.

Parameterization reduces duplication of **data**, not of **scenario visibility**.

---

## Review Gate

Reject spec changes when:

- the spec defines non-trivial local functions;
- the spec duplicates an existing helper;
- the spec contains stability polling or signature logic inline;
- the spec uses `run*Scenario` orchestration helpers;
- matrix tests no longer show action and verification in the test body;
- a new helper was added without checking existing helpers in `src/test/**`.

---

## Main Principle

Specs stay readable because the scenario is visible.

Helpers stay reusable because technical logic lives once in the correct project layer.

Always reuse existing helpers before creating new ones.
